    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d19">

                <pb facs="0108" n="26" xml:id="pg26"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr. Motley</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 144.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 16, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your despatches from No. 90, of the 9th ultimo, to No. 100, of the 24th of
                    the same month, with the exception of No. 98, which has not yet come to
                    hand.</p>
                <p>Your observations upon the fall of Richmond, and the military events which
                    immediately succeeded the occupation of the insurgent capital, are extremely
                    interesting and instructive.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Lothrop Motley</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., Vienna.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
